,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":82.490325961,"data":"2. Provide the landlord with all the necessary documents, such as a copy of the lease agreement, a copy of the rent payment schedule, and any other relevant documents.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":82.491719711,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":82.492795348,"data":"3. Provide the landlord with a copy of the eviction notice, which should include the reason for eviction and the date of the eviction.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":82.493792173,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":82.494751528,"data":"4. If the landlord refuses to accept the notice, you can file a lawsuit in court to evict the tenant.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":82.495714824,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":82.496657187,"data":"5. If the landlord does not respond to your eviction notice within 14 days, you can file a lawsuit in court to evict the tenant.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":82.497515514,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":82.498372888,"data":"6. If the landlord still refuses to accept the notice, you can file a lawsuit in court to evict the tenant and seek damages for any losses incurred.\n"}
