,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1066.227044547,"data":"Response A:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1066.228337242,"data":"If you're considering stopping taking antidepressants, here are some steps you can take:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1066.229477576,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1066.230505358,"data":"1. Talk to your doctor: Before stopping antidepressants, it's important to talk to your doctor. They can help you determine the best course of action for you.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1066.231402578,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1066.232323343,"data":"2. Gradually reduce the dose: If you're taking antidepressants, gradually reduce the dose over time. This can help prevent withdrawal symptoms.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1066.233106409,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1066.234048354,"data":"3. Monitor your symptoms: Keep track of your symptoms and report any changes to your doctor. This can help them adjust your medication and adjust your dosage.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1066.234986428,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1066.235846403,"data":"4. Avoid stress: Stress can make it harder to feel good, so try to avoid stressful situations and find ways to manage them.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1066.236718322,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1066.237624256,"data":"5. Consider alternative treatments: If you're not responding to antidepressants, there are alternative treatments available, such as cognitive-behavioral therapy or medication-assisted treatment.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1066.238534115,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1066.239362404,"data":"Response B:\n"}
