,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.053779066,"data":"I will be having a party tomorrow, and plan on drinking with friends. I believe my tolerance is relatively high, but know the symptoms in the next day are never nice to me. Specifically, I tend to be prone to nausea the day after, and headaches. I've previously tried to sip water between the alcoholic drinks, but still experienced nausea that night. What should I do specifically to alleviate these symptoms? Is my situation different from that of others?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.055139191,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.056039282,"data":"Response A:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.056944181,"data":"It is possible that your situation is different from others. However, there are some general tips that can help alleviate nausea and headaches after drinking:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.058041308,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.059136541,"data":"1. Drink water: Sipping water between alcoholic drinks can help to dilute the alcohol and reduce the risk of nausea and headaches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.060213271,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.061305412,"data":"2. Take a break: If you feel like you need to drink more, take a break from drinking and drink water instead.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.062377731,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.063302698,"data":"3. Eat something: Eating something light and easy to digest can help to reduce nausea and headaches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.064240732,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.065201472,"data":"4. Avoid alcohol: If you have a history of alcoholism or are prone to nausea and headaches after drinking, it may be best to avoid alcohol altogether.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.066727898,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.067527065,"data":"5. Medication: If you have severe symptoms, you may want to consider taking medication to alleviate nausea and headaches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.068544036,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.069711858,"data":"It is always best to consult with a healthcare professional if you have any concerns about your drinking habits or symptoms.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.071296058,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.072084269,"data":"Response B:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.073296183,"data":"It's great that you're aware of your tolerance and the symptoms you're experiencing. Here are some suggestions to help alleviate your nausea and headaches:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.074273728,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.075164674,"data":"1. Sip water: Sipping water between alcoholic drinks can help dilute the alcohol and reduce the risk of nausea. Drink a glass of water before each alcoholic drink to help prevent nausea.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.075948039,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.076838296,"data":"2. Drink slowly: Drinking slowly can help you avoid feeling the effects of alcohol on your stomach and head. Take small sips and drink slowly to avoid feeling the effects of alcohol on your stomach.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.077635808,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.07844408,"data":"3. Avoid alcohol: If you're experiencing nausea and headaches, it's best to avoid alcohol altogether. Alcohol can exacerbate nausea and headaches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.079170597,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.080067696,"data":"4. Take a break: If you're experiencing nausea and headaches, it's best to take a break from drinking and rest for a few hours. This can help you recover from the effects of alcohol.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.080872329,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.081717949,"data":"5. Consider medication: If you're experiencing severe nausea and headaches, it may be helpful to consider medication. Speak with your doctor about the options available to you.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.082525788,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1314.083320555,"data":"Overall, it's important to listen to your body and take care of yourself during your party. Drinking responsibly and taking breaks can help you avoid the symptoms you're experiencing and enjoy your party.\n"}
