,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.62769317,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.628747247,"data":"2. Community: Small businesses often have a strong sense of community and a strong sense of ownership. They may have a loyal customer base, and they may be more likely to offer discounts or promotions to their customers.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.629744645,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.630811374,"data":"3. Quality: Small businesses may be more likely to offer high-quality products or services, which can be more satisfying to customers. They may also have a more diverse range of products or services, which can be more appealing to customers.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.631800539,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.632653717,"data":"4. Cost: While prices may be higher for small businesses, they may offer a more affordable option for customers who are on a budget. They may also offer a more personalized approach to customer service, which can be more satisfying to customers.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.633559922,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.634494909,"data":"5. Trust: Small businesses may be more likely to have a strong reputation for quality and customer service, which can be more satisfying to customers. They may also be more likely to offer discounts or promotions to their customers, which can be more\n"}
