,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.636316179,"data":"Response B:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.637149742,"data":"There are several reasons why someone might prefer to shop at a small, locally-owned business instead of a large chain store, even if the prices are higher:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.637971355,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.638811679,"data":"1. Personalization: Small businesses often have a more personalized approach to customer service, which can be more satisfying to customers who value personalization.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.639573832,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.640385524,"data":"2. Quality: Small businesses may have a more in-depth understanding of their customers' needs and preferences, which can lead to higher-quality products or services.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.641257595,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.642065717,"data":"3. Community: Small businesses often have a strong sense of community and are more likely to be involved in their local community. This can lead to a more positive reputation and a more loyal customer base.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.642886937,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.643765179,"data":"4. Cost: While larger chains may have higher prices, small businesses may be able to offer lower prices due to economies of scale and lower overhead costs.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.644600325,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1400.645429319,"data":"5. Convenience: Small businesses may be able to offer more convenient shopping options, such as in-store pickup or delivery, which can be especially important for customers who may not have the time or resources to shop online.\n"}
