,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1426.296512473,"data":"question about Computer architecture and organization \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1426.297756561,"data":"for 6 marks\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1426.298880323,"data":"what in general terms is the distinction between computer organization and computer architecture ?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1426.300045893,"data":"give answer in full sentence points if possible\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1426.301265182,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1426.302484493,"data":"Response A:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1426.303278682,"data":"The distinction between computer organization and computer architecture is that computer organization refers to the physical layout and design of the computer, while computer architecture refers to the underlying hardware and software components that make up the computer. In general, computer architecture is concerned with the design and implementation of the computer's hardware and software components, while computer organization is concerned with the physical layout and design of the computer.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1426.304099525,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1426.304942215,"data":"Response B:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1426.305832548,"data":"The distinction between computer organization and computer architecture is that computer organization refers to the physical layout and design of the computer, while computer architecture refers to the underlying hardware and software components that make up the computer system. In general, computer architecture determines the overall structure and functionality of the computer, while computer organization determines the physical layout and design of the computer. For example, a computer with a 64-bit processor and a 32-bit operating system is an example of a computer architecture, while a computer with a 1 GHz processor and a 64-bit operating system is an example of a computer organization.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1426.306611316,"data":"\n"}
