,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.126295011,"data":"List the layers of the TCP/IP model and for each layer identify one protocol.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.127160544,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.128320291,"data":"Response A:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.129063261,"data":"The TCP/IP model is divided into seven layers, each with its own protocol. Here are the layers and their protocols:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.129977412,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.130939786,"data":"1. Physical Layer: This layer is responsible for transmitting data over physical media such as wires, cables, and optical fibers. The protocol used is the Physical Layer protocol.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.131997856,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.133093085,"data":"2. Data Link Layer: This layer is responsible for transmitting data over a physical medium, but it also ensures that the data is transmitted reliably. The protocol used is the Data Link Layer protocol.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.133996563,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.134993408,"data":"3. Network Layer: This layer is responsible for routing data packets between different networks. The protocol used is the Network Layer protocol.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.135897326,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.13680658,"data":"4. Transport Layer: This layer is responsible for ensuring that data packets are delivered reliably and in a timely manner. The protocol used is the Transport Layer protocol.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.137760216,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.138635815,"data":"5. Session Layer: This layer is responsible for establishing and maintaining connections between applications. The protocol used is the Session Layer protocol.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.139589372,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.14055903,"data":"6. Presentation Layer: This layer is responsible for converting data from one format to another. The protocol used is the Presentation Layer protocol.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.141570275,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.142543339,"data":"7. Application Layer: This layer is responsible for providing end-to-end services to applications. The protocol used is the Application Layer protocol.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1647.143355775,"data":"\n"}
