,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.742910359,"data":"Instruction:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.743986329,"data":"Can you help me figure out how to sew a button on a shirt?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.74497681,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.745872834,"data":"Response A:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.746883618,"data":"Sure, I'd be happy to help you with that. Here are the steps to sew a button on a shirt:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.747728977,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.748862059,"data":"Materials:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.750059717,"data":"- Button\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.751258422,"data":"- Scissors\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.752447735,"data":"- Pins\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.753433042,"data":"- Thread\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.754367791,"data":"- Fabric glue\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.755413102,"data":"- Iron and ironing board\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.756600606,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.75773528,"data":"Step 1: Cut the button\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.758976302,"data":"Cut the button in half, making sure the buttons are the same size. You can use scissors to cut the button in half, or you can use a button maker to make the buttons for you.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.760099899,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.761308564,"data":"Step 2: Pin the buttons\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.762488463,"data":"Place the buttons on the shirt, making sure they are centered and facing the right way. Pin the buttons in place with a pin.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.763672374,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.764793329,"data":"Step 3: Iron the buttons\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.766109874,"data":"Take the ironing board and gently press the buttons onto the shirt, making sure they are centered and facing the right way. You can use a button iron to press the buttons, or you can use a heat gun to press the buttons.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.767181027,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.768421575,"data":"Step 4: Apply fabric glue\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.769564955,"data":"Apply a small amount of fabric glue to the back of the button, making sure it is evenly distributed. You can use a small amount of fabric glue to apply it, or you can use a fabric glue gun to apply it.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.77072708,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.771923098,"data":"Step 5: Sew the buttons\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.773005587,"data":"Using a sewing machine,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.774117783,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.775250048,"data":"Response B:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.77605898,"data":"Sure, I can definitely help you with that. Here are the steps to sew a button on a shirt:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.776864323,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.777690209,"data":"1. Choose the right button: Look for a button that fits well and is easy to sew. You can find buttons at most department stores or online.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.778486117,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.779285277,"data":"2. Cut the button: Cut the button to the desired size and shape. You can use a utility knife or scissors to cut the button.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.780066231,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.780873972,"data":"3. Pin the button: Pin the button onto the shirt using a pin. Make sure it is centered and straight.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.781675928,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.782451244,"data":"4. Sew the button: Sew the button onto the shirt using a sewing machine or a seam ripper. You can use a straight stitch or a diagonal stitch depending on the button you are using.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.783193088,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.783916542,"data":"5. Trim the excess: Trim any excess fabric around the button to create a neat edge.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.78475832,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.785545692,"data":"6. Iron the shirt: Iron the shirt to make sure the button is secure and the fabric is smooth.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.786291073,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.787025383,"data":"That's it! You should now have a button sewn onto your shirt.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1841.787860013,"data":"\n"}
