,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1940.919262449,"data":"Instruction:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1940.920498386,"data":"What is the difference betwean interpreted compiled and JIT-ed programming language, can you also tell me some benefits of each type of language?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1940.921673972,"data":"Can you give me at least 3 examples from each of these categories of programming languages?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1940.922836222,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1940.924062116,"data":"Response A:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1940.925238785,"data":"Interpreted compiled programming languages and JIT-ed programming languages are two different approaches to programming. Here's a brief comparison of the two:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1940.926467222,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1940.927651511,"data":"Interpreted compiled programming languages:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1940.928853971,"data":"- They are compiled into machine code before execution.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1940.930145179,"data":"- The code is executed directly by the computer's processor.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1940.931443206,"data":"- They are faster than JIT-ed programming languages because they don't have to go through the interpreter.\n"}
