,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2141.509042964,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2141.509930039,"data":"For example, if two individuals hold different beliefs about the morality of abortion, they may have different opinions about the issue and may not be able to agree on how to approach it. This lack of consistency can lead to a lack of understanding of the issues at hand and can result in a lack of support for the issue.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2141.510938678,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2141.511915381,"data":"In addition to personal beliefs, cultural differences can also contribute to inconsistencies in ideological thinking. For example, individuals from different cultural backgrounds may have different beliefs about the role of religion in society, which can lead to a lack of coherence and consistency in their thinking.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2141.512832724,"data":"\n"}
