,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2227.30781075,"data":"The KeyHole series of spy-satellites were developed by the US National Reconnaissance Office (NRO) in the 1960s and 1970s. They were designed to monitor the activities of enemy forces and gather intelligence on their movements. The KeyHole series was the first of its kind and was used to track enemy aircraft and ships, as well as gather information on enemy communications and military operations.\n"}
