,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2227.310670089,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2227.311749466,"data":"The KeyHole series were still active in the 1980s and 1990s, but their capabilities were limited. They were not able to track enemy aircraft or ships, and their data was not transmitted back to NRO's headquarters. The satellites were also not able to transmit real-time data, which made them less useful for intelligence gathering.\n"}
