,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2227.317016022,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2227.317876911,"data":"The KeyHole series were operational from 1968 to 1979, and were designed to provide a wide-angle view of the Earth's surface. They were equipped with a variety of instruments, including cameras, radar, and optical telescopes, which allowed them to capture high-resolution images and data. The KeyHole series was eventually retired in 1979, and their capabilities were eventually replaced by more modern and advanced spy-satellites.\n"}
