,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2311.438709138,"data":"what is the Infinite banking concept?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2311.439522841,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2311.440404547,"data":"Response A:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2311.441170995,"data":"The Infinite banking concept refers to the idea that the banking system should be designed to provide a continuous and uninterrupted flow of credit and money to the economy, without any constraints or limitations. This means that banks should be able to lend money to businesses and individuals at any time, and should not be subject to any restrictions or limitations on their operations.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2311.441972037,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2311.442811055,"data":"The concept was first proposed by the British economist John Maynard Keynes in the 1930s, and has since become a cornerstone of modern banking theory. The idea is based on the belief that the economy should be able to grow and expand without any major disruptions or shocks, and that banks should be able to provide a stable and predictable source of credit and funding.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2311.443699902,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2311.444521853,"data":"Infinite banking is often contrasted with traditional banking, which is limited by the availability of credit and the ability to lend money only to those who can afford it. The infinite banking concept suggests that banks should be able to provide credit and funding to everyone, regardless of their ability to pay back the loans.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2311.44527082,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2311.446089178,"data":"The infinite banking concept has been widely adopted in modern banking systems, and has been seen as a key driver of economic growth and development. It has also been criticized for potentially leading to a lack of competition and a concentration of power in the hands of a few large\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2311.446879278,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2311.447645442,"data":"Response B:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2311.448459376,"data":"The Infinite banking concept refers to the idea that all financial transactions are infinite, meaning that there is no end to the amount of money that can be created or spent. This concept is based on the idea that money is a universal currency that can be used to buy anything, regardless of the amount of money involved. It is also based on the idea that money can be created and spent without any limits or restrictions. This concept is often associated with the idea of a global economy and the idea that money can be used to create wealth and prosperity for all people.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2311.44926575,"data":"\n"}
