,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2463.513535739,"data":"Instruction:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2463.514480296,"data":"Let's assume a friend had a very bad day. What could be a way to cheer them up without making it too obvious and help them keep their mind off things?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2463.515462482,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2463.517302708,"data":"Response A:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2463.517341234,"data":"1. Encourage them to take a walk: A quick walk outside can help clear their mind and give them a break from the stress of their day. You can also suggest a fun activity like going for a run or taking a hike.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2463.518092338,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2463.519257066,"data":"2. Share a joke: A funny joke can lighten the mood and help them forget about their problems. You can also suggest a joke that is relevant to their current situation.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2463.520528413,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2463.521647797,"data":"3. Offer a hug: A hug can help them feel loved and supported. You can also suggest a hug that is a little more intimate, like a cuddle.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2463.522850126,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2463.524037069,"data":"4. Share a story: A story can help them feel connected to someone else and can also provide a sense of comfort. You can suggest a story that is relatable to their current situation.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2463.525290981,"data":"\n"}
